%N A055397 Maximum population of an n X n stable pattern in Conway's Game of Life.
%H A055397 Geoffrey Chu and Peter J. Stuckey, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.artint.2012.02.001">A complete solution to the Maximum Density Still Life Problem</a>, Artif. Intel. 184-185 (2012), 1-16.
%H A055397 Geoffrey Chu, Karen Elizabeth Petrie, and Neil Yorke-Smith , <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-84996-217-9_10">Constraint Programming to Solve Maximal Density Still Life</a>, in Game of Life Cellular Automata, Chapter 10, A. Adamatzky, Springer-UK (2010), 99-114.
%H A055397 Geoffrey Chu, Peter J. Stuckey, and Maria Garcia de la Banda , <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-04244-7_22">Using relaxations in Maximum Density Still Life</a>, in Proc. 15th Intl. Conf. on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (2009), Lect. Notes Comp. Sci 5732, 258-273.
%H A055397 Venkata Pushpak Teja Menta, <a href="https://openreview.net/forum?id=4LBYPzoSUW">Verifier-Clean Connected Still Lifes Across All Box Sizes: A Complete CP-SAT Encoding with Annealing Polish</a>, OpenReview.net (2026). See pp. 2, 6.
%H A055397 Stephen Silver, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20160712023902/http://www.argentum.freeserve.co.uk/dense.htm">Dense Stable Patterns</a>
%F A055397 a(n) = (n^2)/2 + O(n).
%F A055397 For n >= 55, floor(n^2/2 + 17*n/27 - 2) <= a(n) <= ceiling(n^2/2 + 17*n/27 - 2), which gives all values of this sequence within +- 1.
%e A055397 a(3) = 6 because a ship has 6 cells and no other 3 X 3 stable pattern has more.
%K A055397 nonn,changed
%O A055397 1,2
%A A055397 _Stephen A. Silver_, Jun 25 2000
%E A055397 a(11)-a(27) from _Nathaniel Johnston_, May 15 2011, based on table in Chu et al.
%E A055397 a(28)-a(53) from _Nathaniel Johnston_, Nov 27 2013, based on work by Chu et al.
%E A055397 a(24) and a(26) corrected, based on Table 7 of Chu and Stuckey (2012), by _Siddhartha Mahajan_, Jul 27 2026
